[{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q1","number":1,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions require the use of Double Angle Formulae, Reversing the Chain Rule, Integration by Parts, Integration by Substitution and A-Level Maths Partial Fractions</strong></p><p>For each of the following pairs of parametric equations, the region is bounded by the given curve, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and any line if given. The region is rotated around the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis until a solid of revolution is generated. In each case, determine the volume of the solid generated giving your answer in exact form:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=t^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2t^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=t^3+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=28\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sin t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{\\cos t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\sqrt4=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_0^2(t^3)^2(2t)\\,dt\n=\\pi\\int_0^22t^7\\,dt\n=\\frac\\pi4[t^8]_0^2=64\\pi\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\sqrt[3]8=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_0^2(t^2)^2(6t^2)\\,dt\n=6\\pi\\int_0^2t^6\\,dt\n=\\frac{768\\pi}{7}\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=28\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t^3+1=28\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_0^3(t^2)^2(3t^2)\\,dt\n=3\\pi\\int_0^3t^6\\,dt\n=\\frac{6561\\pi}{7}\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_0^{\\pi/2}(\\sqrt{\\cos t})^2\\cos t\\,dt\n=\\pi\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\cos^2t\\,dt.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos^2t=\\frac12(1+\\cos2t)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\left[\\frac t2+\\frac14\\sin2t\\right]_0^{\\pi/2}\n=\\frac{\\pi^2}{4}\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>For each of the following pairs of parametric equations, the region is bounded by the given curve, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and any line if given. The region is rotated around the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis until a solid of revolution is generated. In each case, determine the volume of the solid generated giving your answer in exact form:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sqrt{1-t^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1+t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\\cos t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\tan t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sin^2t\\sqrt{\\cos t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\cos t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1+t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dt=2t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2=1-t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_0^1(1-t^2)(2t)\\,dt\n=\\pi\\left[t^2-\\frac12t^4\\right]_0^1\n=\\frac\\pi2\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\pi/4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_0^{\\pi/4}(2\\cos t)^2\\sec^2t\\,dt\n=4\\pi\\int_0^{\\pi/4}dt=\\pi^2\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Here <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2=\\sin^4t\\cos t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dt=\\sin t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin^5t\\cos t\\,dt\n=\\frac\\pi6[\\sin^6t]_0^{\\pi/2}\n=\\frac\\pi6\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=e^{\\frac12t}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=\\sqrt{t-2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>A region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is enclosed by the curve, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=e^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=e^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that the volume of the solid generated when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rotated about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi e^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=e^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=e^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Also <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx/dt=\\frac12e^{t/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y^2=t-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\int_4^6(t-2)\\frac12e^{t/2}\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac\\pi2\\left[2e^{t/2}(t-2)-4e^{t/2}\\right]_4^6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =2\\pi e^3\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\sqrt{\\ln|t+1|}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=t^2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>A region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is enclosed by the curve, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that the volume of the solid generated when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rotated about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi(8\\ln2-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\\leq t\\leq3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2=\\ln(t+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dt=2t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_1^32t\\ln(t+1)\\,dt.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integration by parts gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\left[t^2\\ln(t+1)-\\int\\frac{t^2}{t+1}\\,dt\\right]_1^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\left[t^2\\ln(t+1)-\\frac12t^2+t-\\ln(t+1)\\right]_1^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =2\\pi(8\\ln2-1)\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>A funnel may be modelled by a curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> defined parametrically by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\frac4t\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=\\ln t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The region bounded by the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, and the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\ln4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rotated through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis to form a solid. All lengths are measured in centimetres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the exact volume of the funnel.</p></li><li><p>State a limitation of the model.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\ln4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2=16/t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dt=1/t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_1^4\\frac{16}{t^3}\\,dt\n=\\pi\\left[-\\frac8{t^2}\\right]_1^4\n=\\frac{15\\pi}{2}\\text{ cm}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The model assumes that the funnel has no thickness and perfectly follows the curve.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=1-\\cos t\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=\\sqrt{\\sin t}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and is shown in the diagram below. A region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is enclosed by the curve and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.36/questions/assets/FMQ_2.36_q6_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Determine the volume of the solid generated when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rotated about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The curve meets the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{\\sin t}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The non-zero endpoint in the stated interval is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx/dt=\\sin t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y^2=\\sin t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\int_0^\\pi\\sin^2t\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\int_0^\\pi\\left(\\frac12-\\frac12\\cos2t\\right)dt\n=\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\sqrt t\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=e^t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Given that the volume of the solid generated when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rotated about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi(3e^4+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2=t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dt=e^t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\int_0^kt e^t\\,dt\n=\\pi[te^t-e^t]_0^k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi((k-1)e^k+1).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Equating this with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi(3e^4+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k-1)e^k=3e^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q8","number":8,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>By using the substitution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\cos^3\\theta\\,d\\theta=\\sin\\theta-\\frac13\\sin^3\\theta+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Find the volume formed by the region enclosed by the curve defined by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac\\pi2\\leq\\theta\\leq\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when rotated <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians across the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Question 9: Calculus of Hyperbolic Functions and Improper Integrals</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"du=\\cos\\theta\\,d\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos^3\\theta=\\cos\\theta(1-\\sin^2\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\cos^3\\theta\\,d\\theta=\\int(1-u^2)\\,du\n=u-\\frac13u^3+c\n=\\sin\\theta-\\frac13\\sin^3\\theta+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Using the result in part (a),</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2}\\cos^3\\theta\\,d\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\left[\\sin\\theta-\\frac13\\sin^3\\theta\\right]_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2}\n=\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is defined by parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\cosh t-\\sinh t\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=\\cosh t+\\sinh t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\leq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. An unbounded region is formed when the region between the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and the line corresponding to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rotated through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the curve can be expressed as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac1x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence, determine the exact volume of the solid formed.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh^2t-\\sinh^2t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nxy=(\\cosh t-\\sinh t)(\\cosh t+\\sinh t)=1,\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1/x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\leq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=e^{-t}\\geq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV=\\pi\\int_1^\\infty\\frac{1}{x^2}\\,dx\n=\\pi\\left[-\\frac1x\\right]_1^\\infty\n=\\pi\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The inside surface of a nozzle is modelled by the parametric curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=ae^{-t}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=bt^2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive constants. The curve is rotated <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis. The bottom of the nozzle sits on the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis. All lengths are measured in centimetres. It is required that the nozzle has diameter 4 cm and a height of 3 cm.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> according to the model.</p></li><li><p>Find the volume of the nozzle giving your answer to three significant figures.</p></li><li><p>State a limitation of the model.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> because the diameter is 4 cm. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4b=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=3/4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2e^{-t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dt=\\frac32t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\int_0^2(2e^{-t})^2\\frac32t\\,dt\n=6\\pi\\int_0^2te^{-2t}\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =6\\pi\\left[-\\frac12te^{-2t}-\\frac14e^{-2t}\\right]_0^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{3\\pi}{2}(1-5e^{-4})\\approx4.28\\text{ cm}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The model assumes the nozzle has no thickness and that its inner surface exactly follows the curve.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>A glass ornament is made by rotating a smooth curve about a vertical axis. The profile of a glass ornament is modelled by a curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> defined parametrically by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\sqrt{t^2-1}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=t+\\ln t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\\leq t\\leq3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. All lengths are measured in centimetres. The region between the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis is rotated through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis to form a solid.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the maximum diameter of the ornament, giving your answer to the nearest mm.</p></li><li><p>Find the maximum height of the ornament, giving your answer to the nearest mm.</p></li><li><p>Find the volume of the glass ornament to three significant figures.</p></li><li><p>The ornament is made from glass with density <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2.5\\text{ g cm}^{-3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the mass of the ornament, giving your answer to two significant figures.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The maximum value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sqrt{t^2-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> occurs at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore the maximum diameter is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2\\sqrt{3^2-1}=4\\sqrt2\\approx5.7\\text{ cm}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>to the nearest millimetre.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The minimum height is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1+\\ln1=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and the maximum is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3+\\ln3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The ornament's maximum height is therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+\\ln3\\approx3.1\\text{ cm}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the nearest millimetre.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2=t^2-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dt=1+1/t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =\\pi\\int_1^3(t^2-1)\\left(1+\\frac1t\\right)dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\left[\\frac13t^3+\\frac12t^2-t-\\ln t\\right]_1^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\approx30.1\\text{ cm}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Using the unrounded volume, the mass is approximately <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2.5(30.1)=75.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> g, which is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"75\" data-display=\"false\"></span> g to two significant figures.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\frac2t\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=\\frac{t^2}{e^t}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The maximum of the curve is at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant to be found.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.36/questions/assets/FMQ_2.36_q12_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>A region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is enclosed by the curve, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Show that the volume of the solid generated when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is rotated about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\pi\\left(\\frac{29}{18e^{4/3}}-\\frac{13}{2e^4}\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Differentiating <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=t^2e^{-t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=te^{-t}(2-t).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The maximum occurs at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2/t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4/e^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(1,4/e^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx/dt=-2t^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y^2=t^4e^{-2t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV =2\\pi\\int_{2/3}^2t^2e^{-2t}\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\left[-\\frac12t^2e^{-2t}-\\frac12te^{-2t}-\\frac14e^{-2t}\\right]_{2/3}^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\left(\\frac{29}{18e^{4/3}}-\\frac{13}{2e^4}\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.36-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\ln(t-3)\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=\\frac8{\\sqrt t}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.36/questions/assets/FMQ_2.36_q13_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The shaded region is enclosed by the curve, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and the line which passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the origin. Determine the exact volume of the solid generated when the shaded region is rotated about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> radians.</p>","steps":["<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\ln13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The line from the origin to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x/\\ln13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The volume generated by the curve is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV_C =\\pi\\int_4^{16}\\left(\\frac8{\\sqrt t}\\right)^2\\frac1{t-3}\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\pi\\int_4^{16}\\frac{64}{t(t-3)}\\,dt\n=\\frac{64\\pi}{3}\\ln\\frac{13}{4}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The volume generated by the straight line is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV_L=\\pi\\int_0^{\\ln13}\\left(\\frac{2x}{\\ln13}\\right)^2dx\n=\\frac{4\\pi\\ln13}{3}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The region's volume is therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nV_C-V_L=\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\left(16\\ln\\frac{13}{4}-\\ln13\\right)\\text{ units}^3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]